mantle rm535
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_magnus_stanmore
title crumbs against the new moon
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child humour=merry
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk uses_crumbs_to_subtract_a_debt_with_each_bite
likes warm_bread riddles fresh_straw first_snow
dislikes haggling drizzle
fears having_to_explain_the_unticked_column
hopes seeing_a_whole_page_settled
topics pastimes +0.7 prices +0.5 food +0.4 dreams +0.3
styles comfort=playful gossip=sly refuse=precise tease=merry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# arranges crumbs into two columns and subtracts a debt with each bite.

words
oath! = Nick my last notch | Blot my splendid answer
saying! = A crumb repaid still tastes of bread | Two half riddles make a longer afternoon
grub = a warm loaf heel | a steaming crust
square = a ruled square | a little box
mark = a crooked tick | a neat dot
penny = a dull penny | a small round copper
moon = a slender crescent | a half-hidden moon
sum = a troublesome figure | a tidy reckoning
stake = a promised crumb | a twist of clean straw
bunch = a straw twist | a little bundle
riddle = a question with a hinge | a crooked little puzzle
rain = penny-sized drops | a tiresome drizzle
rest = a gap between sums | an empty square
dust = the floury end | a spray of crumbs

any
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I'd pay extra for an honest price if doing so didn't spoil the whole exercise.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A House factor can give even a trifling sum an uncomfortably long shadow.
opinion festivals for 1 : Dancing costs one's breath and never sends a second demand.
opinion dole for 1 : If a hungry wolf owes nothing for breakfast, why invent a new column?
opinion road mixed 1 : A useful road should run both ways for the same fare.
opinion times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : When every bite gets dearer, a crumb becomes a fairly serious denomination.

any
line greet : A welcome, free of charge today. | I've saved a blank square for company.
line greet.return : Consider that greeting returned in full.
line again.open : Back before I rubbed out your first mark.
line farewell : Take a little credit for a pleasant visit.
line farewell.return : Your farewell earns an equal one from me.
line react.news : Give me the puzzle end of that news.
line react.news.new : That's one fresh mark on the page.
line react.news.known : I recognise those figures in a different order.
line react.news.doubt : Who checked the sum before passing it along?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Surely even this account deserves a kinder reckoning.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That deserves a splendid fat tick.
line ask.how : Has your side of the page stayed sunny?
line answer.how : One figure out, but I've several excellent suspects.
line sympathise : Sit with me. Unhappy sums can wait.
line reassure : One unsettled square needn't spoil a page.
line refuse : I owe my next hour to something else.
line accept_decline : I'll put a clean stroke through the invitation.
line preclose : My figures will multiply if I leave them untended.
line accept_preclose : You may go with a thoroughly clear column.
line ack : Right, both sides agree.

young
line greet : Welcome to my crumb exchange.
line farewell : Don't count the moon twice tonight.
line react.news : I can listen without charging an entrance crumb.

adolescent
line greet : Welcome from the side still doing the arithmetic.
line farewell : May your evening leave a credit.
line ask.how : How steep has the day's account grown?

grown
line greet : Beside my figures I've kept a visitor's spot.
line farewell : May your evening's reckoning bring some ease.
line react.news : I'll hear the terms before inspecting the arithmetic.

young

scene exchange2
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What spends itself by growing smaller? I've an answer. | I change one word in a riddle.
b : A candle? | Does that make it new?
a : Good. Mine was supper. We can both have a point. | It makes yesterday's clever answer wonderfully embarrassing.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My crumb bank charges interest in heat. | A loaf heel makes a capital counting board.
b : How do you pay that? | Where are the figures?
a : Eat before the crust goes cold. | Gone. My appetite has passed its examination.

scene exchange4
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've got five counters that smell of a stable. | Twist straw twice and it holds a promise.
b : Are they straws? | How long?
a : If you can guess the sixth you can have it. | Till one of us remembers where the coin went.

scene exchange5
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first snow covers all yesterday's sums. | I like catching a flake on a copper.
b : A clean start? | Does that add value?
a : On the paving. My head still keeps the account. | A whole drop if I act quickly.

scene exchange6
when topic=day self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd buy one price and keep it forever. | Haggling over a crumb takes longer than eating it.
b : What price? | Who wins?
a : The first honest one I met. | The sparrow, usually.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Drizzle puts extra dots among my figures. | Rain that won't commit ought to owe us interest.
b : Do they add anything? | Payable in what?
a : A quite false impression of diligence. | Sunny minutes after tea.

scene exchange8
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At lessons I favour questions with one penny missing. | I count out a difficult sum upon my fingers.
b : Why missing? | What if it needs more?
a : It gives the answer somewhere to go. | That's what obliging toes were made for.

scene exchange9
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd lend #self.friend# my best riddle. | I keep a friendly debt in a round box.
b : Can riddles be returned? | An actual coin?
a : Improved, if somebody finds a second answer. | A joke I promised to finish.

scene exchange10
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a moon that went backwards on request. | I could settle every debt with a perfect riddle.
b : Why backwards? | Who'd accept that?
a : A few extra nights improve a deadline. | Somebody quite a bit like me, I hope.

scene exchange11
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A factor's figures look bigger upside down. | I remember what I'm owed to the last crumb.
b : Have you tried turning them over? | And what you owe?
a : Only the page, and it didn't help. | Unfortunately my memory works both directions.

scene exchange12
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Heights have enough stairs for counting practice. | A slope can teach subtraction.
b : How many? | How?
a : I lost my place when a particularly fine smell came out a window. | Walk downhill eating bread one mouthful per landing.

scene exchange13
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let visitors guess my easiest riddle first. | I offer directions in whole turns.
b : Is that kind? | No half turns?
a : It makes them stay for the dreadful second one. | Half a turn would point you back at me.

scene exchange14
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give thanks for a lost penny found. | I say my quiet words before breakfast.
b : Even if it wasn't yours? | Why before?
a : Especially then. Returning it would improve two accounts. | Afterwards another slice occupies most of my thoughts.

adolescent

scene exchange16
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I write the answer before constructing the trap. | A riddle about debt needs careful wording.
b : Is that fair? | Or it sounds unkind?
a : It is my only defence against trapping myself. | Or it sounds regrettably like an invoice.

scene exchange17
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I now put dates beside little loans. | A promise should say exactly what comes back.
b : Does that help friendships? | Even a borrowed book?
a : It saves two friends from inventing different winters. | Particularly a borrowed book with crumbs in its spine.

scene exchange18
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh snow is the sole ledger I enjoy spoiling. | I count snowfall by the covered steps.
b : With your boots? | Does that measure depth?
a : With several splendid circuits no accountant could balance. | It measures how long I can put off sweeping.

scene exchange19
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I divide warm bread before beginning a sum. | A slice shared now needn't be repaid in summer.
b : To get neat fractions? | A free slice?
a : To keep the best crust clear of ink. | An edible distinction between sharing and lending.

scene exchange20
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to set one last debt to rights privately. | Some evenings I count down to the dark moon.
b : A grand secret? | Looking forward to it?
a : An ordinary obligation becomes grand enough without an audience. | Looking attentively towards it, which is another calculation.

scene exchange21
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can show #self.friend# an unfinished puzzle. | A friend gets to challenge my arithmetic.
b : A risk to your reputation? | Even when it's right?
a : An investment in a far better punchline. | Checking is half the pleasure.

grown

scene exchange23
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A riddle with two good answers deserves two prizes. | I still keep one unanswerable question.
b : What are the prizes? | What for?
a : The pleasure of hearing both well defended. | To rescue a dull evening from easy certainty.

scene exchange24
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave ordinary kindness out of formal accounts. | A paid debt gets a line through the figure.
b : Do you forget it? | Why leave it legible?
a : Precisely the opposite. I remember how freely it was given. | A cleared obligation deserves a visible ending.

scene exchange25
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry shelf is the first requirement of a ledger. | I keep bread on a separate shelf now.
b : Before a lock? | An accounting principle?
a : A thief may never come. Drizzle visits reliably. | A hard lesson in what fresh crumbs do to ink.

scene exchange26
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I share a loaf by asking which end looks best. | Warm bread can quiet an argument over a small sum.
b : Both choose the heel? | Does it settle the debt?
a : Then the heel itself becomes a matter for division. | It allows two mouths to chew before answering.

scene exchange27
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fine rain costs more paper than a downpour. | I give a wet account time to dry.
b : Why more? | Before you read it?
a : In a downpour even an optimist puts the figures away. | Before I decide which digits are merely raindrops.

scene exchange28
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# a balance before signing it. | A friend needn't enter every favour in my book.
b : For an audit? | Do you enter them?
a : For a second pair of unhurried eyes. | Some go straight to memory, ink-free.

scene exchange29
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When bread is dear a small loan needs plain terms. | I offer a smaller share before extending the date.
b : Why more than usual? | Why that order?
a : Because repaying confusion can cost a meal. | It lets the borrower choose what is manageable.

scene exchange30
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the turns uphill when my mind is crowded. | A high window makes a fine observatory.
b : Do the sums help? | For the moon?
a : They give the rest of my thoughts room to settle. | And for the weather that may hide it on a due date.

scene exchange31
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Winter accounts leave room for fuel. | I mark the first snowfall in my book.
b : What goes in spring's column? | As an expense?
a : A new sheet and the pleasure of open shutters. | As a delight worth writing down.

scene exchange32
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A traveller's loan wants a clear meeting spot. | I keep enough for the return fare separate.
b : More than a date? | Too cautious?
a : A date without a place makes very poor company. | I like my further adventures to be voluntary.

scene exchange33
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New arrivals sometimes ask when the day's market settles. | I offer a stranger the plain version of my riddle.
b : Which sign should they watch? | Saving the hard one?
a : Watch the bread buyers, not the loudest price. | Until I know there's a taste for it.

scene exchange34
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember counting with crumbs before using ink. | The sums I feared most were often very small.
b : Any advantages? | Why fear them?
a : A clean slate was particularly agreeable. | An approaching date can throw quite a shadow.

story tale1 [topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles]
  : I wrote a puzzle with the answer tucked under a bread crust.
  : By the second question the hiding place had been eaten.
  b : Was the answer eaten too?
  : Only a corner. Enough remained to suggest a much better answer than mine.

story tale2 [topic=weather self.likes=first_snow]
  : I drew a figure in fresh snow and carried on down the path.
  : When I looked back a small track had turned my zero into an elaborate eight.
  b : Did you accept the correction?
  : Only on the understanding that the next snowfall would erase the evidence.

story tale3 [topic=prices]
  : I marked a debt with a knot and its repayment with a second knot.
  : By evening I could remember the figure perfectly and couldn't undo the string.
  b : Did you keep both knots?
  : I kept the string as a model of an unnecessarily complicated arrangement.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A new square for the morning. | The sums are asleep yet.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Look at that thin moon. | Close the book on the dark.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Those dots don't count. | Dry corner for the tally.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sunset, payable in crumbs. | Only the crust remains outstanding.
dlg resident.hub : There's still room for one enquiry in my good column.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you can claim a return visit on the account.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Ask while the moon is available as a witness.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I prefer a precise question to a demand without a figure.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons take up their proper share of my page. Riddles fill the margins.
dlg resident.job : I keep the arithmetic honest, especially when it wants to be amusing.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : I've entered this among the day's news. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Someone reckons #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I haven't balanced that account.
dlg resident.bye : May your next obligation be a pleasantly small one.

graft resident.hub
choice Can a crumb really pay a debt? -> crumb_question
node crumb_question
say If you agreed to lend a crumb, certainly. Confusing a crumb with a penny is where most of the interesting trouble begins.
free
choice What about a promised joke? -> crumb_question_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node crumb_question_again
say Repay it by making the lender laugh. A solemn explanation will only increase the balance.
choice I'll leave that column open. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
